# Review: plugin-connector

The spec still describes the pre-rename model. The code calls an Integration a `Connection`
(`org.dxos.type.connection` in `@dxos/link`), an IntegrationProvider a `Connector`, and it has moved the
`targets` array out of the record into separate `Cursor` objects (`spec.kind: 'external'`) that point at
the connection's access token. So the types, the auth button, the provider picker and
`SetIntegrationTargets` are `diverged`, even though most of the behaviour they describe still exists.

The flow behaviour is solid. The coordinator drafts the token and connection, writes a `localStorage`
snapshot for every flow, calls EDGE `/oauth/initiate`, opens a popup or a new tab, finalizes on
`postMessage` or on the `/redirect/oauth` startup module, sets `AccessToken.parent`, runs
`onTokenCreated` (failures are caught and logged), then navigates. `reconcileCursors` is well tested.
Most coordinator paths have no test: none of `connector-coordinator.ts` is exercised, so most reqs are
`untested`, and seven of the ten scenarios have no automation. The real gaps are smaller. A failure
message only raises a toast and leaves the pending entry in the map. `CustomTokenDialog` has no generic
raw-token fallback, so it shows an error when a connector has no `credentialForm`. And
`SetIntegrationTargets` is not a registered operation.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict IntegrationTarget: Targets are separate Cursor objects with an external spec, not rows on the record.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/link/src/Cursor.ts#Cursor, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/link/src/Cursor.ts#ExternalSpec]
  note: '`Cursor` carries `max`/`min` (for `cursor`), `lastTick` (for `lastSyncAt`) and `lastError`; its `ExternalSpec` holds `source` (the AccessToken ref), `target`, `externalId`, `label`, `options` and `snapshots`. A binding is found by token, not by an array on the connection.'
```

```mdl
verdict Integration: The record is Connection (org.dxos.type.connection), with no targets or snapshots.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/link/src/Connection.ts#Connection]
  note: Fields are `name`, `connectorId` (for `providerId`), an optional `accessToken` and an optional `mcp` endpoint. `targets` became Cursor objects and `snapshots` moved onto each cursor's spec.
```

